  "summary": "Vulnerability in the Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK product of Oracle Java SE (component: Compiler).  Supported…",
  "details": "Vulnerability in the Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK product of Oracle Java SE (component: Compiler).  Supported versions that are affected are Oracle Java SE: 21.0.13.0.3, 25.0.5.0.3 and  27.0.1.0.3; Oracle GraalVM for JDK: 21.0.13.0.3. Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via multiple protocols to compromise Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK.  Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized ability to cause a hang or frequently repeatable crash (complete DOS) of Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK as well as  unauthorized update, insert or delete access to some of Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK accessible data and  unauthorized read access to a subset of Oracle Java SE, Oracle GraalVM for JDK accessible data. Note: This vulnerability can only be exploited by supplying data to APIs in the specified Component without using Untrusted Java Web Start applications or Untrusted Java applets, such as through a web service. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 7.0 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts).  CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H).",
